    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d722">

                <pb facs="0788" n="778" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg778"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/10–144:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-27T19:00:00-04:00">October 27, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3677. Since MEW has instructed British Minister in Bern to join you in
                    approaching Swiss Minister of Foreign Affairs along lines of <pb facs="0789"
                        n="779" xml:id="pg779"/> Department’s 8178, October 6, 6 p.m. to London,
                    repeated to Bern as Department’s 3509 [<hi rendition="#italic">3433</hi>], and
                    subsequent telegrams, the Department wonders if <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >démarche</hi> has been made (London’s 8956, October 19, 8 p.m. to
                        Department<anchor n="31" xml:id="d722-f1"/> which London repeated to Bern).
                    If not please make <hi rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> as soon as possible and
                    cable Department urgently the result of this action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
